cff-version: 1.2.0
message: If you use this work, please cite it as below.
title: "Integrated prime-counting errors for prime moduli"
abstract: "The integrated prime-counting error changes sign arbitrarily far out in every reduced residue class modulo each prime from 11 through 10,009. Under Dirichlet GRH, a positive proportion of classes change sign at every prime modulus from 11 onwards. Under the same hypothesis the forward test in class 1,258 modulo 10,009 needs exactly twelve progression terms."
